    "summary": "High‑energy Europe ’72 set with soaring Greatest Story and epic Other One jam",
    "blurb": "The show bursts open with a soaring Greatest Story Ever Told and a tight Deal. Highlights include an explosive Truckin' > The Other One sequence featuring the hidden “Feeling Groovy” jam, Jerry's pedal‑steel solo on Looks Like Rain, and a smoking Good Lovin'. Overall the performance is high‑energy with strong band cohesion throughout.",
    "review": "April 11, 1972 at Newcastle City Hall finds the Dead in top form during their Europe ’72 trek. The first set launches with an inspired Greatest Story Ever Told that sets a bright tone, and by the time they hit Deal the band is already locked in. A standout moment arrives late in the set when Truckin' erupts into a loose‑yet‑tight jam that segues seamlessly into an expansive Other One suite – complete with a hidden “Feeling Groovy” interlude that showcases Phil’s jazzy bass lines and Keith’s soaring keys. Jerry’s vocal power shines on Good Lovin', while his pedal‑steel work on Looks Like Rain adds a sweet, country‑tinged texture rarely heard live. The rhythm section drives the momentum forward, with Bill (Billy) delivering an intense drum pulse that underpins the improvisations. Closing the night with a gentle Brokedown Palace encore, the band leaves Newcastle buzzing from a performance that balances exploratory jams with tight songcraft.",
